[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571305794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101084#issuecomment-2571305794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101084","id":2571305794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZQwNC","user":{"login":"aXu-AP","id":1621768,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE3Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621768?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP","html_url":"https://github.com/aXu-AP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aXu-AP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-04T13:30:35Z","updated_at":"2025-01-04T13:30:35Z","body":"I think this is what's happening: a capsule's `radius` cannot be more than half of `height` (in which case the shape is a circle). Setting `height` limits the `radius` to a correct value (and vice versa, if you test your code but switch the order, `height` should be 200). Try setting these values in editor, you will observe the same result.\n\nNote that this differs from Godot 3, where `height` referred to the center part of the capsule. I guess that was unintuitive and therefore was changed to current behaviour, where `height` is the total height (but it makes `radius` and `height` somewhat interdependent).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repo